{"nodes": [{"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security", "label": "Security", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_threat_model", "label": "Threat Model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Threat model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assume the attacker controls every function argument, transaction ordering and timing, every account that does not require a signature, contracts that mimic your interface, and the shape of on-chain state they can legally create, including entry counts and TTLs. They can even extend your entries' TTLs."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_delegatecall", "label": "No delegatecall", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "What the platform rules out", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contracts cannot execute foreign bytecode in their own context, so proxy-style delegatecall hijacks do not exist."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_reentrancy", "label": "No Reentrancy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "What the platform rules out", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The host blocks reentrant calls, direct or indirect, on normal cross-contract paths. External calls remain failure, budget, and side-effect boundaries, so state updates should still be ordered deliberately."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_host_auth_replay", "label": "Host-managed Auth Replay Protection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "What the platform rules out", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nonces and expirations on authorization entries are enforced by the host, not by contract code."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_authorization", "label": "Authorization", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "What the platform rules out", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "require_auth is opt-in, so forgetting it is the failure mode to hunt for. The right address is the one with policy authority loaded from storage, not a caller-supplied parameter."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_missing_authorization", "label": "Missing Authorization", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "1. Missing authorization", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every privileged path needs require_auth on the address that holds policy authority. require_auth on an arbitrary caller-supplied address proves control of that address and nothing about permission."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_auth_replay", "label": "Auth Replay Through Middleware", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "2. Auth replay through middleware (missing outer `require_auth`)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If a user has pre-signed an auth tree that includes an inner token.transfer, anyone can call a middleware entrypoint that never itself authorizes the user and consume that signature. Re-authorize at every layer that exercises an address's authority. This is the most common real-world auth bug."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_reinitialization", "label": "Reinitialization Attacks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "3. Reinitialization attacks", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A guarded initialize matters only when you do not use __constructor, which cannot re-run. Without a check-and-set flag, anyone can call initialize and capture admin."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_arbitrary_contract_calls", "label": "Arbitrary Contract Calls", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "4. Arbitrary contract calls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A user-supplied contract address is arbitrary code. It can fail, trap, burn budget, emit misleading events, or call other contracts. It cannot re-enter you. Allowlist external contracts."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_integer_overflow", "label": "Integer Overflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "5. Integer overflow/underflow", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "overflow-checks = true panics on overflow in the release profile, but explicit checked math fails cleaner and survives a profile mistake. An unchecked negative i128 transfer withdraws from the recipient. Use checked methods for 256-bit types on protocol 26 and later."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_storage_key_collisions", "label": "Storage Key Collisions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "6. Storage key collisions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Untyped keys can silently overwrite unrelated data. Always use a #[contracttype] key enum."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_check_then_act", "label": "Check-then-act Races", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "7. Check-then-act races", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "State can change between transactions, so checks and state changes must be atomic in one invocation, and swaps should take a caller-supplied min_out. approve overwrites, so reducing a non-zero allowance can be front-run; approve to 0 first or use exact-amount auth."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_ttl", "label": "TTL and Archival Failures", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "8. TTL and archival failures", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A temporary entry can disappear permanently, and a persistent entry can archive and add restoration friction. Separately, anyone can extend any entry via ExtendFootprintTTLOp, so expiry is not a permission boundary. Store an explicit deadline in the value and check it."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_cross_contract_returns", "label": "Untrusted Cross-contract Returns", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "9. Trusting cross-contract return values", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Validate data from external contracts. Allowlist oracles, sanity-check magnitudes, and enforce freshness."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_resource_exhaustion", "label": "Resource Exhaustion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "10. Resource exhaustion / fee griefing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A function whose worst-case cost on attacker-shaped input exceeds network limits denies service to legitimate users. Cap loops over user-controlled collections, per-iteration storage or events, and signature counts in __check_auth, and keep footprints small."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_custom_accounts", "label": "Custom Account Pitfalls", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "11. Custom account (`__check_auth`) pitfalls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verify signature_payload itself. Enforce policies from auth_contexts; ignoring them makes a policy wallet decorative. CAP-71 get_delegated_signers returns unsanitized user input, so verify each address is a registered delegate before delegate_auth."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_token_consumer", "label": "Token-consumer Review", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Token-consumer review (AMMs, vaults, escrows, lenders)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Any contract that takes a token address must assume native XLM's SAC, a wrapped classic asset's SAC, or a custom contract. Permissionless tokens bring arbitrary-call risk. Do not assume 7 decimals. Re-check the received amount after transfer when fee-on-transfer tokens matter. Survive missing trustlines, AUTH_REQUIRED, frozen accounts, and issuer clawback. transfer_from must authorize the spender, not from, and standard token events must be emitted."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_scout", "label": "Scout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CoinFabrik Scout (cargo scout-audit) ships 20+ detectors, including missing overflow checks, unprotected WASM update, unrestricted transfers, unsafe unwrap, and DoS-unbounded ops, and can emit SARIF for CI."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_oz_detectors", "label": "OpenZeppelin Security Detectors", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The OpenZeppelin Soroban security detectors SDK includes auth_missing, unchecked_ft_transfer, and improper TTL extension, plus a framework for custom detectors."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_certora_sunbeam", "label": "Certora Sunbeam", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Tooling", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Certora Sunbeam expresses specs as Rust macros and operates on WASM bytecode."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_audit_bank", "label": "Soroban Audit Bank", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Audits and bounties", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Stellar Development Foundation subsidizes audits for SCF-funded protocols through Audit Bank. Follow-up audits trigger at TVL milestones."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_immunefi", "label": "Immunefi Stellar", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Audits and bounties", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Immunefi's Stellar program pays up to $250K for core, SDK, and CLI vulnerabilities. A proof of concept is required, and testing must use local forks only."}, {"id": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_immunefi_oz", "label": "Immunefi OpenZeppelin on Stellar", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Audits and bounties", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Immunefi pays up to $25K for the audited OpenZeppelin contracts library on Stellar."}], "edges": [{"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_skill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Security", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_development", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Security", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_testing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Security", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_threat_model", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_ttl", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Threat model", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_threat_model", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_arbitrary_contract_calls", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "Threat model", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_missing_authorization", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_development_authorization", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "1. Missing authorization", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_missing_authorization", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_authorization", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "1. Missing authorization", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_auth_replay", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_missing_authorization", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "2. Auth replay through middleware (missing outer `require_auth`)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_auth_replay", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_development_auth_trees", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "2. Auth replay through middleware (missing outer `require_auth`)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_auth_replay", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_development_require_auth", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".agents/skills/smart-contracts/security.md", "source_location": "2. Auth replay through middleware (missing outer `require_auth`)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_security_reinitialization", "target": "agents_skills_smart_contracts_development_constructor", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_sc